The heavy ions or polarized protons can be accelerated to nearly the speed of light and circulate in opposite directions in the two storage rings. They can collide with each other at the 6 interaction points along the RHIC rings. Among these interaction points, four experiments were built: STAR, PHENIX, PHOTOS and BRAHMS. If enumerate the positions of these experiments by the clock positions, STAR experiment is located at 6 o'clock position and near the injection points of AGS to RHIC transfer line, PHENIX at 8 o'clock, PHOBOS at 10 o'clock and BRAHMS at 2 o'clock. Today, STAR experiment is the only RHIC experiment that operates.

