### Number of Equivalent MB Events and Trigger Bias Calculation

In Run15 pp and pAu, \(\Upsilon\) is studied with the BHT2*BBCMB triggered events. In this analysis, the number of equivalent MB events and the trigger bias are calculated for both \(\mathrm{J/\Psi}\) and \(\Upsilon\). The cross section of \(\mathrm{J/\Psi}\) or \(\Upsilon\) can be obtained by equation Equation 3.7.

The \(\mathrm{J/\psi}\) or \(\Upsilon\) cross section can be obtained by:

\[\sigma_{\mathrm{particle}}=\frac{\sigma_{\mathrm{MB}}}{\mathrm{N}_{\mathrm{MB }}^{\mathrm{eqv.}}\epsilon_{\mathrm{MB}}^{\mathrm{goodvtx}}}*\frac{\mathrm{N}_ {\mathrm{particle}}^{\mathrm{trav}}}{\mathrm{Acc.}\times\epsilon_{\mathrm{particle }}^{\mathrm{Trig}}\epsilon_{\mathrm{particle}}^{\mathrm{trk}}\epsilon_{ \mathrm{particle}}^{\mathrm{eID}}}*\frac{\epsilon_{\mathrm{MB}}^{\mathrm{ BBC}}\epsilon_{\mathrm{MB}}^{\mathrm{goodvtx}}}{\epsilon_{\mathrm{particle }}^{\mathrm{BBC}}\epsilon_{\mathrm{particle}}^{\mathrm{goodvtx}}} \tag{3.7}\]

Where:

* \(\sigma_{\mathrm{MB}}\) is the NSD cross section for p+p collisions and total cross section for p+Au collisions.
* \(\mathrm{N}_{\mathrm{MB}}^{\mathrm{eqv.}}\) is the number of equivalent BBCMB events corresponding to the analyzed BHT2*BBCMB events.
* \(\epsilon_{\mathrm{MB}}^{\mathrm{goodvtx}}\) is the good vertex efficiency in normal MB events.
* \(\mathrm{N}_{\mathrm{particle}}^{\mathrm{raw}}\) is the number of raw counts of \(\mathrm{J/\Psi}\) or \(\Upsilon\) from real data.
* Acc. is the acceptance of TPC, EMC and the momentum cuts on electrons.
* \(\epsilon_{\mathrm{particle}}^{\mathrm{Trig}}\), \(\epsilon_{\mathrm{particle}}^{\mathrm{trk}}\) and \(\epsilon_{\mathrm{particle}}^{\mathrm{eID}}\) are the BHT2 trigger efficiency, tracking efficiency and electron identification efficiency, which are obtained from the embedding samples.
* \(\epsilon_{\mathrm{MB}}^{\mathrm{BBC}}\) is the BBC efficiency in normal MB events.
* \(\epsilon_{\mathrm{particle}}^{\mathrm{BBC}}\) is the BBC efficiency in the particle (\(\mathrm{J/\Psi}\) or \(\Upsilon\)) events.
* \(\epsilon_{\mathrm{particle}}^{\mathrm{goodvtx}}\) is the good vertex efficiency in the particle (\(\mathrm{J/\Psi}\) or \(\Upsilon\)) events.

* \(\frac{\epsilon_{\text{MB}}^{\text{BBC}}\epsilon_{\text{MB}}^{\text{goodvtx}}}{ \epsilon_{\text{particle}}^{\text{BBC}}\epsilon_{\text{particle}}^{\text{ goodvtx}}}\) is defined as the trigger bias factor in this analysis.

The number of equivalent MB events can be calculated in section 3.4.1. The trigger bias factor and the related efficiency can be obtained by analyze the simulated data of PYTHIA + GEANT + Zero-Bias simulation as discussed in section 3.4.3.1 and section 3.4.3.2.

