The number of equivalent MB events can be calculated based on the formula Equation 4.2, here the \(N_{\text{MB}}^{\text{eqv.}}(\text{online})\) is the number of equivalent MB events while BBCMB trigger and BHT2*BBCMB trigger are all active. The total number of \(N_{\text{MB}}^{\text{eqv.}}(\text{online})\) is calculated by the sum over all runs.

\[N_{\text{MB}}^{\text{eqv.}}(\text{online})=\sum_{\text{irun}}[N_{\text{BBCMB}} ^{\text{recorded}}(|\text{Vz}|<200)\frac{\text{LIVETIME}_{\text{BHT2}}\text{PS}_ {\text{BBCMB}}}{\text{LIVETIME}_{\text{BBCMB}}\text{PS}_{\text{BHT2}}}](\text{ irun}) \tag{3.8}\]

