### Systematic uncertainties of \(\Upsilon\) measurements in Run15 pp and pAu

The systematic uncertainties of \(\Upsilon\) cross section measurements in Run15 pp and Run15 pAu are obtained in different sources:

* Fitting Ranges: the default fitting range is 7.0-14.0 \(\mathrm{\text{\text{\text{GeV}}}\kern-0.8pt/c^{2}}\), the fitting ranges are changed to 6.6-14.0, 7.4-14.0, 7.0-13.6, 7.0-13.8, 6.8-13.8 \(\mathrm{\text{\text{GeV}}}\kern-0.8pt/c^{2}\) and obtain cross sections, take the maximum difference relative to default cross section as the systematic uncertainty from the fitting range.
* Binning Width: the default bin width is 0.2 \(\mathrm{\text{\text{GeV}}}\kern-0.8pt/c^{2}\), changed to 0.16 \(\mathrm{\text{\text{GeV}}}\kern-0.8pt/c^{2}\) and 0.4 \(\mathrm{\text{\text{GeV}}}\kern-0.8pt/c^{2}\), take the maximum difference relative to default cross section as the systematic uncertainty from the binning width.
* \(\Upsilon\) Templates: The default template Width and the Shift factor are obtained from the fitting of smeared signals. The smeared template rely on the fitted width and mean of real \(\mathrm{J}/\psi\), so the width and mean of \(\Upsilon\) templates are varied to cover the fitted statistical uncertainty of \(\mathrm{J}/\psi\) mean and width. The widths of \(\Upsilon\) templates are changed by \(\pm 5\%\), and the shift of the mean of \(\Upsilon\) templates are changed \(\pm 10\%\).
* \(\mathrm{\text{\text{B}}}\kern-0.8pt\overline{\mathrm{\text{B}}}\) (BB) and Drell-Yan (DY) Templates: The BB and DY shapes are from the PYTHIA simulation with the detector efficiency embedded. The default PYTHIA settings in this analysis for the BB and DY simulation are from the PHENIX tuned settings which could well describe the measured BB and DY production at RHIC energy. There is another PYTHIA settings tuned to match results of di-lepton analysis. We take the differenceof our physics results based on BB and DY shaped from this two PYTHIA settings as a systematic uncertainty of BB and DY shapes.
* \(\Upsilon(1\mbox{S})\):\(\Upsilon(2\mbox{S})\):\(\Upsilon(3\mbox{S})\) relative ratio: The default value of these relative ratios between each \(\Upsilon\) state are from the world wild average value (1:0.275:0.128) for both Run15pp and Run15Au, the ratios are changed to (1:0.275:0) for Run15pp systematic uncertainty. The CMS measured ratios (1:0.22:0.08) in pPb collisions [46] are used for the for the systematic uncertainty estimation of Run15 pAu.
* Tracking "nHitsFits and nHitsDedx" Cuts: The default cuts used in Run15 pp and pAu is "nHitsFits \(\geq\) 25 and nHitsDedx \(\geq\) 15", the cuts are changed to "nHitsFits \(\geq\) 20 and nHitsDedx \(\geq\) 10" for the systematic uncertainty calculation.
* Dca cut: the default cut is "dca \(<\) 1.5 cm", the cuts are changed to "dca \(<\) 1.25 cm" and "dca\(<\)1.75 cm" for the systematic uncertainty calculation.
* Trigger Threshold Adc0 cut: the default Adc0 cut is "Adc0 \(\geq\) 300", the cut is changed to "Adc0 \(\geq\) 303" for the systematic uncertainty calculation.
* E/p cut: the default cut is "0.7 \(<\) E/p \(<\) 2.0", the cut is changed to "0.8 \(<\) E/p \(<\) 1.8" and "0.6 \(<\) E/p \(<\) 2.5" systematic uncertainty calculation.
* n\(\sigma_{\rm e}\) cut: the mean and \(\sigma\) of n\(\sigma_{\rm e}\) are changed up and down according to statistical uncertainties of the mean and \(\sigma\) from fitting * BEMC matching "zDist and phiDist" cut: the default cut is "zDist \(<\) 10 and phiDist \(<\) 1", these cuts are changed to "zDist \(<\) 11 and phiDist \(<\) 1.1" and "zDist \(<\) 9 and phiDist \(<\) 0.9" for systematic uncertainty calculation.
* \(\Upsilon\)\(\mathrm{p_{T}}\) curve parameter "T" value: The default value of T is 1.127 is obtained from the fitting of previous STAR \(\Upsilon\) measurement in U+U collisions [48], and this value is changed to 1.1 and 1.3 for systematic uncertainty calculation.
* The uncertainty of geometrical acceptance (for p+p and p+Au collisions): The uncertainty of the polarization of \(\Upsilon\) mesons, it will be studied later. **The other common systematic uncertainties:**
* The uncertainty from the NSD cross section measurement (for p+p collisions): \(\sigma_{\mathrm{NSD}}\) = \(30\pm 2.4\) mb
* The uncertainty from the Glauber model parameter (for p+Au collisions): \(\mathrm{N_{coll}}\) = 4.7\(\pm\)0.3 [73]
* The uncertainty from the Trigger Bias factor: TrigBias(pp) = 0.4800 \(\pm\) 0.0144, TrigBias(pAu) = 0.5338 \(\pm\) 0.0267

